.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "wrap-ansi [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.com/chalk/wrap-ansi.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.com/chalk/wrap-ansi) [![Coverage Status](https://coveralls.io/repos/github/chalk/wrap-ansi/badge.svg?branch=master)](https://coveralls.io/github/chalk/wrap-ansi?branch=master)"
.PP
.RS 4
Wordwrap a string with \fRANSI escape codes\fP 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install wrap\-ansi
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
const chalk = require('chalk');
const wrapAnsi = require('wrap\-ansi');

const input = 'The quick brown ' + chalk\&.red('fox jumped over ') +
    'the lazy ' + chalk\&.green('dog and then ran away with the unicorn\&.');

console\&.log(wrapAnsi(input, 20));
.fi
.PP

.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "wrapAnsi(string, columns, options?)"
Wrap words to the specified column width\&.
.SS "string"
Type: \fRstring\fP

.PP
String with ANSI escape codes\&. Like one styled by \fR\fRchalk\fP\fP\&. Newline characters will be normalized to \fR\\n\fP\&.
.SS "columns"
Type: \fRnumber\fP

.PP
Number of columns to wrap the text to\&.
.SS "options"
Type: \fRobject\fP
.SS "hard"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRfalse\fP

.PP
By default the wrap is soft, meaning long words may extend past the column width\&. Setting this to \fRtrue\fP will make it hard wrap at the column width\&.
.SS "wordWrap"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
By default, an attempt is made to split words at spaces, ensuring that they don't extend past the configured columns\&. If wordWrap is \fRfalse\fP, each column will instead be completely filled splitting words as necessary\&.
.SS "trim"
Type: \fRboolean\fP\\ Default: \fRtrue\fP

.PP
Whitespace on all lines is removed by default\&. Set this option to \fRfalse\fP if you don't want to trim\&.
